Session: 98385d6036f340f09c9cb7713c6a3399
Goal: Build the Send / hold page (web/sendhold.html, currently a stub) of the static explorer in this repository, following the existing patterns in cubs_edge_lab/web_export.py, web/app.js, web/format.js and tests/test_explorer_e2e.py. The spec is summarized here; it is binding.

Integrity rules (the existing guards apply to this page too):
- Every rendered number is a value copied by the export from research/*.json by JSON pointer, tagged data-src="file#pointer", shown in the shared display format with a full-value <details>. The export never computes, rounds or derives a statistic. The DOM scan must cover this page.
- Text quoted from research/*.md is copied by the export verbatim, by exact line match, with its file and line recorded as its source; a test fails if the line is no longer present verbatim.
- Do not edit research/ or data/. Do not invent values or wording that states a result.
- No model values by default (spec rule 3): do not show predicted P(safe), mean_p_safe, flagged hold counts, runs left values, or any Cubs model value outside the elements named below. Extend the default-visible pointer allowlist test to this page.

Page content, in this order:
1. Verdict panel: the primary verdict (sendhold_experiment.json /verdict) followed directly by its meaning from meanings.json, then the pre-registered v2-definition verdict (/verdict_v2_preregistered_definition), with the same unmapped-verdict alert guard as the Overview.
2. Criteria tables, one per analysis in sendhold_experiment.json /analyses (v3_primary, v2_preregistered, v3_ambiguous_as_safe, v3_fallback_dropped), each with a caption naming the analysis and its /verdict. Rows: Brier vs constant, calibration slope, runs left, negative control. Each row shows the published estimate, its 95% interval beside it (interval_95 lower and upper), "Met" or "Not met" in text from /passed, the rule text from /rule, and its role. Roles are fixed display copy kept in the export next to MEANINGS (not derived): Brier vs constant = gating; calibration slope = gating; negative control = control; runs left = effect (only read when the gating criteria are met).
   - The runs-left row shows the text "Not interpretable under the NEGATIVE verdict" when that analysis's verdict is NEGATIVE; its estimate, interval and Met/Not met go inside a <details> labeled "Failed-model value (not for decisions)".
   - Under each table: "The verdict follows the pre-registered gating rule, not a count of passes."
   - Beside the Brier row: "The model did not beat a constant guess; the interval includes zero, so this is no evidence of benefit, not evidence of harm. Passing diagnostic rows do not change the verdict."
3. Decision table from sendhold_fit.json /versions/v3/decision_chart/cells: zone group, hit type, outs, speed tercile, n, n_sent, observed send success, p*. No mean_p_safe. Cells with low_n true are marked in text ("low n"). Show min_cell_n and the speed tercile cuts. The table header carries, verbatim, the line "INFERENCE: Any positive estimate is upper-bound-style: sends are selected and the counterfactual for holds is extrapolated." from research/SENDHOLD_EXPERIMENT.md, then: "Sends were selected by the coaches; observed success is not the success rate of held runners or of a different policy. Break-even p* is not a recommendation." Label p* as derived from the 2025 run expectancy. The table scrolls inside its own container.
4. Label counts: per-season label counts under v3 and v2, from whatever per-season label_counts pointers exist in sendhold_experiment.json and sendhold_fit.json. Each count shows its season and label version; do not compute totals.
5. Feasibility summary from sendhold_feasibility.json: /verdict (PARTIAL, through meanings.json), /verdict_reason, /new_requests_used and /ceiling.
6. Limits of this result (mandatory block, tested present): the UNKNOWN lines from research/SENDHOLD_EXPERIMENT.md (verbatim), sendhold_fit.json /unknown, the reduced covariate set as "<sent_out> of <required_sent_out> required" from /analyses/v3_primary/covariate_choice, and the label history v1 to v3 linking to https://github.com/howlcipher/howl-cubs-dogfood/blob/main/experiments/R003-SENDHOLD-DESIGN.md (a link only; no request is made).
7. The existing provenance footer.

Accessibility and layout as on existing pages: table captions, th scope, Met/Not met in text not color, keyboard-reachable <details>, no horizontal page scroll at 320, 375 and 1280 px.

Tests (pytest + Playwright, existing style): export tests for the new selections and verbatim-line copies; DOM scan and allowlist cover this page; verdict and meaning precede the first table (DOM order and bounding box at 375 px); runs-left row text and details label; Met/Not met text matches /passed for every row; the selection caveat is in the decision table header; low n is marked; limits block present; viewport and keyboard checks for this page; the export-drift test passes with the regenerated web/data.

